<title>HONG KONG: Li not buying Sun Fook Kong stake - paper.</title>
<headline>Li not buying Sun Fook Kong stake - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Li Ka-shing, chairman of Cheung Kong (Holdings) Ltd, has decided not to take a stake in construction and civil engineering firm Sun Fook Kong Holdings Ltd, the Hong Kong Economic Journal said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Last week, China Travel International Investment Hong Kong Ltd said it teamed up with Li and Albert Chow to take a stake in Sun Fook Kong.</p>
<p>Li was not immediately available to comment on the newspaper report.</p>
<p>Chow is a former deputy managing director of Cheung Kong and is currently a non-executive director.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
